index 157e6e05..2649fefb 100644
--- a/docs/BACKENDS.md
+++ b/docs/BACKENDS.md
@@ -168,12 +168,24 @@ KV, recurrent state, persistent KVMem statistics and attention score scratch sta
 evaluation or pipelined prompt read, it reclaims expert pages and restores the full workspace before launching
 dependent kernels. Cache growth is limited to 64 MiB per 16 decode calls and retains the configured VRAM reserve.
 
-The initial scope is CUDA VMM, one sequence, no draft/MTP, no frozen expert placement, and no `--stage-read-mib`
+The scope is CUDA VMM, one sequence, no frozen expert placement, and no `--stage-read-mib`
 override. Unsupported configurations log that the feature is inactive. It is off by default. In KVMem's local
 console, the native argument array is `["--elastic-experts"]`; remove it to restore static workspace allocation.
 Live INFO facts expose expert slots/cache MiB and mapped/full elastic workspace MiB. `STRATA_ELASTIC_TRACE=1`
 also records periodic native CUDA free-memory and CPU/GPU expert counters for controlled comparisons.
 
+Managed KVMem MTP with a verification window of 2..4 (one to three draft tokens) supports both elastic flags.
+The retained workspace includes the draft projection and the entire verification window. Drafting reserves
+KV for the full window before writing provisional rows; verification and partial acceptance keep the narrow
+workspace. Expert growth runs only after accepted state commits, once per MTP cycle, so headroom warmup counts
+accepted cycles in this mode. Ordinary multi-token prompts and reads still restore the full workspace.
+Unmanaged speculative decoding remains outside the qualified scope.
+
+`poly_kvmem_mtp_test MODEL.gguf --elastic-experts [--window 2..4] [--no-graphs] [--q8]` checks partial/full
+acceptance against serial native KV/state, exact full/narrow target logits and draft probabilities, cancellation,
+Query/replay, real expert growth and subsequent prompt admission. `--elastic-headroom-test` uses 288 accepted
+cycles with a 512 MiB borrowing ceiling and a 512 MiB physical reserve.
+
 Qualification uses `poly_elastic_test MODEL.gguf [--no-graphs]`: exact native KV/state/statistics preservation
 across map cycles, full versus narrow workspace logits with fixed expert placement, partial-admission rollback,
 real cache growth/reclaim, Pressure and bounded Query/replay. These are functional tests, not recall-quality tests.
